why DECALN is a screen alignment pattern: it overwrites the whole page with E,
why resets the margins to the full screen and homes the cursor. The IND at the
why end is what proves the margins were released - it sits on what would have
why been the bottom margin, so a surviving region would scroll a row blank
why instead of simply moving the cursor down.
stream \e[Hold\r\nrows\r\nhere
stream \e[1;2r
stream \e#8
stream \e[2;1H\eD
cursor 2 0
line EEEE
